LEVEL 11 → 12 — DECODING ROT13


WHAT THIS LEVEL IS ABOUT :

All letters in data.txt have been shifted 13 positions — the ROT13 substitution cipher. Because the alphabet has 26 letters, ROT13 is its own inverse. This level uses the tr (translate) command for character mapping.


APPROACH : 

Reading the file revealed the ROT13-encoded string. I decoded it using:
cat data.txt | tr 'A-Za-z' 'N-ZA-Mn-za-m'

Command Breakdown

Part              Meaning
tr                Translate/substitute characters 
'A-Za-z'          Original character set (all letters)
'N-ZA-Mn-za-m'    ROT13 mapping — shifts each letter by 13

